From: mscharged-port
Subject: Rollback: an overlay's image waits for the steps still predicted
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A rollback cannot go back past a disc read into the match's memory: the
read's buffer and the object waiting for it would go back with the match
while the read goes on. When a captain uses his super ability, the step
starts SuperAbilityOverlay, and the front end reads the captain's picture
(fe/super_abilities/<team>_super_image in art/fe/superabilityUI.res,
174,784 bytes) later in the same frame. The steps that ran with predicted
inputs before it could no longer be corrected (ROLLBACK IMPOSSIBLE): a
desync whenever one of those predictions was wrong. A replay, which runs
the front end as well, could start the read too.

In an offline match logged read by read (Wario against Bowser, five goals
and overtime), these pictures were the only reads into the match's memory
while it was played: the cutscenes load after a goal, when no step
predicts, and the audio's streams read into the audio's own heap.

AsyncImage::Update now issues its read only when the port lets it
(mscharged_rollback_read_waits): not during a replay, nor while a step has
inputs still predicted. While a read waits, no step predicts, so the steps
predicted get their inputs within a round trip and the picture follows a
few frames later. Without RECHARGED_ROLLBACK or RECHARGED_ROLLBACK_TEST
nothing changes.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_rollback.h b/include/mscharged_rollback.h
index 93d0c1c..631c766 100644
--- a/include/mscharged_rollback.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_rollback.h
@@ -46,6 +46,13 @@ bool mscharged_rollback_resimulating(void);
 // after it was undone. Outside tracked steps, everything goes out.
 bool mscharged_rollback_determ_data_new(int frame, const void* data, unsigned size);
 #endif
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// Whether a disc read the front end asks for (an overlay's image) waits: a
+// rollback cannot go back past a read into the match's memory, so none
+// starts while a replay runs or a step has inputs still predicted. While one
+// waits, no step predicts, and the steps predicted get their inputs.
+bool mscharged_rollback_read_waits(void);
+#endif
 // The inputs applied for the step about to run.
 void mscharged_rollback_inputs_applied(const struct MschargedRollbackInputs* inputs);
 // Between two fixed steps of a match, where the rollback saves the match and
